ies within the  story but  structurally once again iraqi decides to  shake things up completely  and in a direction i never thought it  would go while i thought diamond is  unbreakable serve to combine all of the  main narrative attributes of its three  older brother parrots exceptionally well  i personally thought that while the  structure of it was fun i also felt that  while better  than stardust crusader's episodic nature  diamond is unbreakable lacked direction  and a lot of pivotal moments for me  specifically now i want to clarify right  off the bat that that's not necessarily  a bad thing at all  a lot of people enjoy slice of life  hijinks and it worked remarkably  well for that story given how attached  to the characters i became and how  nostalgic i was towards the very end of  that story  however with all of that said and taking  nothing away from diamond is unbreakable  structurally speaking i think golden  wind is much more suited to my personal  sensibilities as a viewer everything  flows together  remarkably well every encounter makes  sense for the narrative and each episode  informs the next jorno wants to climb  the ranks of the mob  empire to gain power and influence over  his struggling town he meets bruno who  fights him after he learns to kill luca  this is a great mini fight by the way he  befriends bruno and then meets his boss  to try to get a job his boss tasks him  with holding this lighter and keeping  the light aflame for 24 hours koichi  causes trouble during this time  because giorno stole his passport they  get into trouble together and fight a  shadow man also a great fight by the way  jordan proves himself to the boss but he  was only doing so so he could get a  chance at assassinating him and he does  so and now he works with bruno  everything flows naturally into the next  main plot point all the while taking the  main cast and every supporting  character's motivations into  consideration  making for me golden wind a prime  examp