s  throughout this arc but not in the same  way he had done so in the past with arcs  like status crusaders and even diamond  is unbreakable to a large extent he  would often establish the goal and make  the means with which they achieve that  goal  known from the very beginning go to  egypt or find the killer etc however  with this one araki opted to create two  separate goals find out the identity of  the boss so they can kill him  and with the second one being discovered  during this particular section  and so while these side stories are  complete stories into and of themselves  in their own respect  they are still very much intrinsically  part of the original ongoing story  building upon material  and setup from the prior episodes for  instance this section begins on the back  of journal's assassination of bruno's  team capo  and as such is built upon the back of  that consequence bruno introduces jorno  to his team and over the course of this  adventure we come to learn about each of  these new characters until we become  intimately familiar with them heck i  even know all of their names and that's  really rare for someone like me  i mean we got bruno fugo mista leon and  narancia  a beautifully italian oh he said it was  so much confidence and still got  it wrong okay hello native italian  speaker can you please tell us how you  pronounce the name of that character in  jojo  naranja thank you despite right now only  being familiar with giorno and  maybe bruno to a lesser extent by the  time this story reached its midpoint i  found that i loved certain members of  this team more than the main character  journal and had a bond established with  all of them similarly to status  crusaders that put a heavy focus on the  side characters golden wind is in all  intents and purposes structured  identically to status crusaders without  the episodic monster of the week type  format through our first introduction to  the team it's clear that they don't  trust journal yet